"""
Quality — fundamentals for the names momentum already surfaced.

Goes in /opt/breakoutscanner/pages/7_Quality.py

WHAT THIS IS, AND WHAT IT DELIBERATELY IS NOT
---------------------------------------------
This page vets a shortlist. It does not screen the universe.

Fundamental data for Indian equities arrives one HTTP request per company.
At 3,046 symbols that is hours, every night, against an endpoint that owes us
nothing. At 20 symbols it is twenty seconds, on demand, when you actually want
it. So the shortlist comes from the snapshot — which already knows RS,
Minervini and breakout state for every stock — and only those names are
looked up.

The cost of that choice, stated plainly: fundamentals arrive AFTER the
shortlist, so they cannot help you find a candidate. They can only confirm or
kill one momentum already found. If you want fundamentals to select rather
than confirm, this is the wrong page and the answer is a nightly job with a
data source that supports bulk access.

MISSING DATA IS SHOWN, NEVER SILENTLY DROPPED
---------------------------------------------
Yahoo's fundamental coverage for Indian smallcaps is thin and unpredictable,
and thin exactly where your breakouts come from. A page that quietly hid the
stocks it could not price would show you a shorter, cleaner, wrong list — the
same failure as the six universe filters and the RS-stored-as-zero bug.

So: every shortlisted stock appears. Fields that are absent read "n/a" and are
counted in the coverage line at the top. Nothing here filters a stock out for
lack of data, and nothing scores a missing field as zero.

QoQ AND YoY
-----------
Both are shown for revenue and for PAT, from the quarterly statements rather
than from a single summary field, because a summary field cannot tell you
whether profit grew faster than sales. It usually can't tell you what it means
either: Yahoo's earningsQuarterlyGrowth is YoY despite the name.

Every percentage is computed from the rupee figure beside it, so any of them
can be checked by hand.

STYLING
-------
CSS copied verbatim from app.py, same as 5_IPO.py and 6_All_NSE.py. It is
duplicated rather than imported because app.py is a Streamlit script and
importing it would execute the whole main scanner as a side effect.
"""

